  "body": "In https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=592158 this situation was given:\n\n``` JavaScript\nvideo.play();\nwindow.setTimeout(() => video.src = \"bbb.mp4\", 0);\n```\n\nEven though `play()` will invoke the [resource selection algorithm](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#concept-media-load-algorithm), by the time the `src` attribute is set, it has already finished running and `networkState` has returned to `HAVE_NOTHING`. Then [media element load algorithm](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#media-element-load-algorithm) will then _not_ reset `paused` back to true, as it does \"If the media element's `networkState` is not set to `NETWORK_EMPTY`\".\n\n(Note that in the initial description of the bug, the descriptions were flipped.)\n\nThe biggest problem with this is that the newly introduced [`play()` promise](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/505) will be rejected even though the play will later succeed. It's also a bit unfortunate that the timing of setting the `src` attribute (or calling `load()`) has the non-obvious side effect, but that's probably not critical.\n\n@mounirlamouri \n",
